{"id":"687ab87fc96f360ede26a0ebef5428a2c0fcce79","axis":"silent","repo":"lestrrat-go/jwx","sha":"687ab87fc96f360ede26a0ebef5428a2c0fcce79","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"BUILD","lines":["@@ -4,6 +4,12 @@ load(\"@rules_go//go:def.bzl\", \"go_library\", \"go_test\")"," # gazelle:prefix github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v4"," # gazelle:go_naming_convention import_alias"," ","+# Scratch directories that are not part of the module. Without these,","+# gazelle walks bazel's own output tree under .gauntlet and rewrites every","+# BUILD file to point at copies of the repo it finds in there.","+# gazelle:exclude .gauntlet","+# gazelle:exclude .tmp","+"," gazelle(name = \"gazelle\")"," "," go_library("],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Changes","lines":["@@ -4,6 +4,18 @@ Changes"," v4 has many incompatibilities with v3. To see the full list of differences between"," v3 and v4, please read the [Changes-v4.md file](./Changes-v4.md). Coding Agents should read [MIGRATION-v4.md](./MICRATION-v4.md)"," ","+UNRELEASED","+  * [jws] Added `jws.WithStrictECDSA(bool)`, a `jws.Sign` option that rejects","+    anything RFC 7518 forbids for an ECDSA signature. Today that is Section","+    3.4's binding of ES256 to P-256, ES384 to P-384, and ES512 to P-521, so","+    signing a P-521 key under `jwa.ES256()` fails instead of producing a JWS","+    that other JOSE implementations reject.","+","+    The default is unchanged: without the option, a mismatched curve and","+    algorithm still sign exactly as before. `jws.Verify` is unaffected either","+    way. `jwt.Sign` callers can reach the option through","+    `jwt.WithSignOption(jws.WithStrictECDSA(true))`. (#2323)","+"," v4.4.0 20 August 2026","   * [jwa][jwk][jws] ML-DSA (FIPS 204) is now implemented natively when jwx is","     built with Go 1.27 or later, where `crypto/mldsa` is part of the standard"],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"agents/docs/packages.md","lines":["@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ JSON Web Signatures per RFC 7515. Sign, verify, parse."," - **Parse(src []byte, ...ParseOption) (*Message, error)** — parse without verification"," - **SplitCompact(src []byte) ([]byte, []byte, []byte, error)** — split compact JWS into parts"," - Key types: `Message`, `Signature`, `Headers`, `KeyProvider`, `KeySink`, `Base64Encoder`","-- Options: `WithKey()`, `WithKeySet()`, `WithVerifyAuto()`, `WithJSON()`, `WithDetachedPayload()`, `WithDetachedPayloadReader()` (streaming variant; single-key, HMAC/RSA/ECDSA only)","+- Options: `WithKey()`, `WithKeySet()`, `WithVerifyAuto()`, `WithJSON()`, `WithDetachedPayload()`, `WithDetachedPayloadReader()` (streaming variant; single-key, HMAC/RSA/ECDSA only), `WithStrictECDSA()` (sign-only; see ECDSA curve binding below)"," - Global/per-call settings: `WithMaxSignatures()` (usable in both `Settings()` and `Parse()`/`ReadFile()`)"," - Registration: `RegisterSigner()`, `RegisterVerifier()`, `RegisterAlgorithmForKeyType()`, `RegisterAlgorithmForCurve()`"," - **AlgorithmsForKey()** — DEPRECATED. Do not use it, and do not add callers. It is the internal helper jwx uses to guess algorithms for a JWKS key with no `alg`, exported only because it always has been. The code now lives in `jws/internal/keyalg` (`keyalg.Candidates`), which everything in the tree calls directly. It works until the next major version and gets no fixes, and the way it picks algorithms must not change (the list still grows when an extension registers, since the tables are an input). Do NOT patch it. It is a one-line wrapper only because `keyalg` still picks the same way it did before deprecation; when that changes, copy the old code back into `AlgorithmsForKey` instead of letting the change through.","@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@ JSON Web Signatures per RFC 7515. Sign, verify, parse."," - Sub-package: `jws/jwsbb` — compact serialization, signing, verification building blocks. The fastjson-backed `Header` probe (`HeaderParse`/`HeaderGet*`/`HeaderHas`) is a thin facade over `jws/internal/jwsbb`, which holds the implementation plus jwx-internal-only helpers not re-exported by the facade (e.g. `HeaderForEachKey`, the header-key enumerator used by `VerifyCompactFast`'s minimal-shape gate)"," - Sub-package: `jws/internal/keyalg` — key-to-algorithm classification. Owns the process-global registration tables behind `RegisterAlgorithmForKeyType`/`RegisterAlgorithmForCurve` (as `RegisterForKeyType`/`RegisterForCurve`), plus `Candidates` (which algorithms a key could be used with), `KeyTypesFor` (reverse lookup), `ValidateEd25519KeyShape`, and the `ErrUnclassifiableKey` sentinel. Registers the builtin algorithms from its own `init()`."," - ML-DSA (go1.27): `mldsa.go` installs a `Signer`/`Verifier` pair per parameter set. Both accept a raw `crypto/mldsa` key or an AKP `jwk.Key`, and both reject a key whose parameter set disagrees with the algorithm. The signature primitives come from `lestrrat-go/dsig` v1.4.0, which owns the algorithm registration.","+- ECDSA curve binding (sign-side, opt-in): `WithStrictECDSA(bool)` is a `SignOption` that rejects a key whose curve disagrees with the ES256/ES384/ES512 algorithm per RFC 7518 Section 3.4. OFF by default — a mismatched pair signs as it always has. Implemented by `jws/internal/jwsbb.RequireECDSACurve`, reached through `signatureBuilder.Build` (both the compact fast path and the JSON path) and `jws.signStreaming`, each gated on `signContext.strictECDSA`. `jws/jwsbb` never checks: it is the raw layer, so its callers own the decision. `jwt` exposes no option of its own; use `jwt.WithSignOption(jws.WithStrictECDSA(true))`, which also takes `jwt.Sign` off its single-option fast path. `jws.Verify`'s key-to-algorithm inference is deliberately untouched and stays permissive. The option name is deliberately broader than the check, to hold any future RFC 7518 ECDSA sign-time rule."," - Files: `jws.go`, `message.go`, `signer.go`, `verifier.go`, `headers.go`, `interface.go`, `errors.go`, `options.go`, `key_provider.go`, `sign_context.go`, `verify_context.go`, `streaming_detached.go`, `mldsa.go` (go1.27)"," - Imports: jwa, jwk, cert, dsig, internal/{base64,json,pool,tokens}"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"internal/jwxtest/jwxtest.go","lines":["@@ -107,8 +107,8 @@ func GenerateEcdsaKey(alg jwa.EllipticCurveAlgorithm) (*ecdsa.PrivateKey, error)"," \treturn ecdsa.GenerateKey(crv, rand.Reader)"," }"," ","-func GenerateEcdsaJwk() (jwk.Key, error) {","-\tkey, err := GenerateEcdsaKey(jwa.P521())","+func GenerateEcdsaJwk(alg jwa.EllipticCurveAlgorithm) (jwk.Key, error) {","+\tkey, err := GenerateEcdsaKey(alg)"," \tif err != nil {"," \t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(`failed to generate ECDSA private key: %w`, err)"," \t}","@@ -121,8 +121,8 @@ func GenerateEcdsaJwk() (jwk.Key, error) {"," \treturn k, nil"," }"," ","-func GenerateEcdsaPublicJwk() (jwk.Key, error) {","-\tkey, err := GenerateEcdsaJwk()","+func GenerateEcdsaPublicJwk(alg jwa.EllipticCurveAlgorithm) (jwk.Key, error) {","+\tkey, err := GenerateEcdsaJwk(alg)"," \tif err != nil {"," \t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(`failed to generate jwk.ECDSAPrivateKey: %w`, err)"," \t}"],"additions":4,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"jwa/BUILD.bazel","lines":["@@ -24,14 +24,17 @@ go_library("," go_test(","     name = \"jwa_test\",","     srcs = [","+        \"builtin_registry_test.go\",","         \"compression_gen_test.go\",","         \"content_encryption_gen_test.go\",","+        \"cross_kind_test.go\",","         \"elliptic_gen_test.go\",","         \"jwa_test.go\",","         \"key_encryption_gen_test.go\",","         \"key_type_gen_test.go\",","         \"mldsa_test.go\",","         \"options_gen_test.go\",","+        \"registry_snapshot_test.go\",","         \"signature_gen_test.go\",","         \"signature_go127_gen_test.go\",","     ],"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"jwe/BUILD.bazel","lines":["@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@ go_test(","         \"aead_tag_length_test.go\",","         \"bench_encrypt_test.go\